# Testing

Unit and integration tests use Vitest. Browser end-to-end tests use Playwright.

## Requirements

- Significant features need tests with the implementation, not as a follow-up wish.
- Tests must be deterministic. No arbitrary sleeps. Wait on conditions, events, or fake timers.
- Do not skip tests without a tracked ticket or documented reason in the test.
- Do not claim commands passed unless they were executed.
- Prefer fakes and fixtures over live network. Mark true integration tests explicitly.
- Tenant tests must prove organization isolation (ID lookup without org context fails; org A cannot read org B), not only the happy path.
- Job handlers and outbox relays need a replay test: the same job twice produces one tenant-visible effect.
- Security fixes need regression tests without exploit payloads.

## Boundaries

- Domain tests should not boot Fastify, Next.js, Redis, or MinIO.
- API tests may use in-process Fastify with test doubles for use cases.
- Persistence tests belong with database infrastructure and must clean up data they create.
- Playwright covers user-visible journeys. It is not a substitute for unit tests of scoring, tenancy, or SBOM parsing.

## Fixtures

- Sample SBOMs must be minimized and free of secrets.
- Do not commit proprietary or customer SBOMs.
- Time-dependent assertions should freeze time to UTC.
